cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Geoenergy: an interactive browser for U.S. energy datasets"
message: "If you use Geoenergy in your research, please cite it, and cite GeoLibre as the platform it is built on."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Xinming
    family-names: Zhang
    alias: Andyzxm
    affiliation: "Department of Geography and Sustainability, University of Tennessee, Knoxville"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Andyzxm/geoenergy"
url: "https://andyzxm.github.io/geoenergy/"
abstract: >-
  Geoenergy is a browser-based map for exploring and analyzing U.S. energy
  infrastructure data: generation, transmission, substations, data centers,
  fuel pipelines, and county-level outage reliability. It is a focused fork of
  GeoLibre, narrowed to energy data and extended with a curated dataset catalog.
keywords:
  - energy geography
  - electric grid
  - GIS
  - geospatial
  - power outages
  - data centers
license: MIT
references:
  - type: software
    title: "GeoLibre: a lightweight, cloud-native GIS platform"
    authors:
      - given-names: Qiusheng
        family-names: Wu
    repository-code: "https://github.com/opengeos/GeoLibre"
    license: MIT
